                                "sense_id": "a6907e91-ed23-3bcf-9b55-b05dad285873",
                                "text": "At times he even seems to accept the Arab racial myth: seldom if ever is any member of a sharifian lineage whose eponymous ancestor originated in the Hadramawt, however long ago, called anything but a Hadrami sharif."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f61ada52-6583-4423-9f0a-77df204b0f37",
                                "sense_id": "a6907e91-ed23-3bcf-9b55-b05dad285873",
                                "text": "One might even speak of a sharifian mini-empire, as the Sa'dids took control of the Saharan trade in gold and slaves, for a brief time as far as Timbuktu in East Africa."
                            }
                        ]
